    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## SETUP (read me first)\n\n**1. Airtable table** — create a table (e.g. `LinkedIn Outreach`) in base `appmn0qxztijCXMQT` with these fields:\n- `profile_id` (Single line text) — the Unipile provider id (`ACoAA...`). This is the match key.\n- `linkedin_url, first_name, last_name, title` (text)\n- `status` (**Single select**) options: `Fresh, Invited, Accepted, First Msg Sent, Follow-up 1 Sent, Follow-up 2 Sent, Replied, Done, Failed` (typecast auto-creates them on first write, but pre-adding is cleaner)\n- `invited_at, accepted_at, first_msg_at, fu1_at, fu2_at, replied_at` (Date w/ time, OR plain text)\n- `chat_id, last_error` (text)\nSeed each lead with `status = Fresh`.\n\n**2. Credentials**\n- Airtable nodes → your Airtable Personal Access Token credential, and set Table on each node (replace `YOUR_TABLE_ID`).\n- HTTP nodes → a **Header Auth** credential `X-API-KEY = <UNIPILE_API_KEY>`.\n\n**3. Constants inlined**: base `https://api17.unipile.com:14713`, `account_id=0oycWCPlQW-X-LP9jEC1_Q`. Change if needed.\n\n**4. Timezone**: the business-hours guard uses the workflow timezone. Set it in this workflow's Settings to your local zone (self-hosted n8n defaults to the server TZ, often UTC).\n\n**5. Concurrency**: if your n8n supports it, set this workflow to max 1 concurrent execution (Settings) so a slow engine tick can't overlap itself. Otherwise the 2-min interval + small batch keeps overlap unlikely.\n\n**6. DEMO timers**: `Decide actions` has `DEMO=true` (2-min waits). Flip to `false` for real day-1/day-2 delays.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 560
      },
      "id": "note-setup",
      "name": "Setup Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-620, -60]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### A) Invite Sender (cron)\nGuarded to Mon-Fri 9-5 (workflow TZ). Picks `Fresh` rows, caps at 25, sends invites (no note, throttled 1/2s). `Invited`, or `Failed` on hard errors. `422 already_invited_recently` is treated as `Invited` (a pending invite already exists), not a failure.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 1180
      },
      "id": "note-a",
      "name": "Lane A Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-20, -230]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### B) Engine (cron, every 2 min) — the ONLY sender\nGuarded to Mon-Fri 9-5. Per row: `Accepted` -> send first message (starts chat, stores `chat_id`) -> `First Msg Sent`; `First Msg Sent`+1d -> FU1; `Follow-up 1 Sent`+1d (chained) -> FU2; `Follow-up 2 Sent` -> `Done`. Skips `Replied/Done/Failed`. If a send fails the row keeps its prior status and retries next tick.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 1640
      },
      "id": "note-b",
      "name": "Lane B Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-20, 150]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### C) Acceptance Recorder (webhook `new_relation`)\nRegister a Unipile USERS webhook -> this URL. Only records state: matches an `Invited` row by `provider_id`, sets `Accepted`. Idempotent (acts only if currently `Invited`). The Engine sends the first message.\n\n**Simulate:** POST `{ \"event\":\"new_relation\", \"account_id\":\"0oycWCPlQW-X-LP9jEC1_Q\", \"user_provider_id\":\"<a profile_id>\", \"user_full_name\":\"Test\" }`",
        "height": 230,
        "width": 1180
      },
      "id": "note-c",
      "name": "Lane C Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-20, 560]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### D) Reply Recorder (webhook new message)\nRegister a Unipile MESSAGING webhook -> this URL. Ignores our own outbound; on a real inbound reply sets `Replied` + `replied_at`, which makes the Engine skip the lead forever. NOT time-guarded (replies recorded 24/7).\n\n**Simulate:** POST `{ \"event\":\"message_received\", \"account_id\":\"0oycWCPlQW-X-LP9jEC1_Q\", \"chat_id\":\"<chat_id on the row>\" }`",
        "height": 230,
        "width": 1180
      },
